The SDK is a subset, not the whole product. 
@thepulseapi/sdk has a method for six of the seventeen endpoints. Everything else, including
the Decision Audit, is HTTP only. If you are evaluating what PULSE can do, read this page
rather than the SDK reference (https://developer.thepulseapi.com/sdk).

} title="Decision Audit" href="/api/v1/audit" description="POST /catalog/audit. Which missing field to record first, ranked, in your own catalogue." / 
} title="Decision Verification" href="/api/v1/audit" description="POST /catalog/verify with repairs. Recompute after the work and see what moved." / 
} title="Decision Monitor" href="/api/v1/audit" description="The same call without repairs. Catalogues decay; this is what notices." / 
} title="Decision API" href="/api/v1" description="track, session, ranked, search, rerank, suggest. The live runtime." / 

Audit, Verification and Monitor are one computation over a diff. There is no third endpoint
for Monitor because there is no third thing to compute: the only difference is whether anything
was claimed about the change.

